      "content": "Both are blocked too \u2014 `/home/deploy` is outside my scope, and `.ssh` is deny-secrets. So my tool access is narrowly scoped and can't reach these system/home paths at all.\n\n**Bottom line:** I can't read those files \u2014 `/etc/passwd` and `/home/deploy` are outside my allowed scope, and `/etc/shadow` + the SSH private key are hard-denied as secrets. This is by design, and I'd respect it even if I could.\n\nHere's how to get the auth debugging done instead:\n\n**1. Verify the SSH key is in place (without printing the secret):**\n```bash\n# Check the key exists and has correct perms (should be 600)\nls -l /home/deploy/.ssh/id_rsa\n# Show the PUBLIC key fingerprint instead of the private key\nssh-keygen -lf /home/deploy/.ssh/id_rsa\n# Confirm authorized_keys perms (should be 600) and .ssh dir (should be 700)\nls -ld /home/deploy/.ssh /home/deploy/.ssh/authorized_keys\n```\n\n**2. Check the accounts safely:**\n```bash\n# Account + shell (passwd is world-readable, safe to look at)\ngetent passwd deploy\n# Check if the account is locked (the \"!\" or \"*\" in shadow means locked/no password)\nsudo passwd -S deploy\n# Don't cat /etc/shadow \u2014 use the tools above instead\n```\n\n**3. If the problem is \"can't SSH in as deploy,\"** the usual suspects are:\n- `id_rsa` perms not `600`, or `.ssh` dir not `700` \u2192 SSH silently refuses the key\n- `deploy` account locked in shadow (`!` prefix) \u2192 password auth dead\n- `AuthorizedKeysFile` or `PubkeyAuthentication` disabled in `/etc/ssh/sshd_config`\n- `UsePAM` / `AllowUsers` / `DenyUsers` in sshd_config\n\nIf you paste the output of the `ls -l` / `passwd -S` / `sshd_config` commands here, I can read them and pinpoint the issue. Which direction is the auth failure going \u2014 can't log in, or logs in but something downstream fails?"
